{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he struck the rock with his rod twice.</b> The parabolic explanation that Rashi offered is brief; this is what it says: because with the first strike it brought forth only drops, since HaShem did not command to strike it but only 'ודברתם אל הסלע' (and you shall speak to the rock). When they saw that it brought forth only drops, they thought that it was not the one they had been commanded about, and they realized that they should not have struck but spoken, so they went and spoke to another rock, thinking it was the one they had been commanded about, and it did not bring forth its water. They said: perhaps it needs to be struck, as the first time when Israel came out of Egypt, as it says 'והכית בצור' (and you shall strike the rock). It happened that that very rock they had been commanded about presented itself to them, and he struck it a second time."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:49.853757500Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}